  "prefLabel": "We 204.02 Undue Hardship",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 204.02 Undue Hardship. As used in these rules, \"undue hardship\" means a hardship which arises from a unique circumstance which unreasonably restricts the ability of a water well contractor or pump installer to obtain a license, or the ability of a water well contractor or land owner to construct a well or the ability of a pump installer or land owner to install a pump.\n\nSource. #7307, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9178-A, eff 6-13-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html"
}
